#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:13
#: 1d5c677e6faa481b983cd4990c676628
msgid "These nodes allow existing ArduPilot supported peripherals to be adapted to the CAN bus as DroneCAN or MSP devices. This also allows for extending the capabilities of the autopilot hardware. Such as allowing I2C devices (e.g. a compass or airspeed) to be located more than 1 meter from the autopilot and enabling up to 32 servo output channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:17
#: cfd6a17f9b6c4b7d87ab95fc878608e5
msgid "They utilize the `AP_Periph <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/Tools/AP_Periph>`__ library to use existing ArduPilot drivers on a supported hardware board. Translating UART, SPI, I2C, or GPIO-based peripheral devices supported by ArduPilot into DroneCAN devices on the CAN bus or MSP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:19
#: 5f2d817811fe473c8e2c4237af2fe2f2
msgid "This provides an easy method to develop integrated DroneCAN peripherals which can be used with ArduPilot or other systems that support DroneCAN."
msgstr ""

